{"id":"mahabharata-12-330","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":330,"title":"त्रिंशदधिकत्रिशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 330 · Krishna's names and forms","summary":{"en":"Krishna says that by his hair he makes the sun and moon, and tells of the names by which he is known, such as Vrishakapi. He tells how Nara took up a blade of grass to stop Rudra and it became a great axe, and ends by telling Arjuna to bow to Hara, lord of Uma.","kn":"ಸೂರ್ಯ-ಚಂದ್ರರನ್ನು ತನ್ನ ಕೂದಲಿನಿಂದ ರೂಪಿಸುತ್ತೇನೆ ಎಂದು ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಹೇಳಿ ವೃಷಾಕಪಿ ಮುಂತಾದ ತನ್ನ ಹೆಸರುಗಳನ್ನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ರುದ್ರನನ್ನು ತಡೆಯಲು ನರ ಹುಲ್ಲಿನ ಕಡ್ಡಿ ಎತ್ತಿದಾಗ ಅದು ಮಹಾ ಕೊಡಲಿಯಾಯಿತು; ಉಮಾಪತಿ ಹರನಿಗೆ ನಮಸ್ಕರಿಸಲು ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कृष्ण कहते हैं कि वे अपने केशों से सूर्य-चन्द्र बनाते हैं और वृषाकपि जैसे अपने नाम बताते हैं। वे बताते हैं कि रुद्र को रोकने के लिए नर ने तिनका उठाया तो वह महान परशु बन गया, और अर्जुन से उमापति हर को नमन करने को कहते हैं।","te":"సూర్యచంద్రులను తన కేశాలతో సృష్టిస్తానని కృష్ణుడు చెప్పి వృషాకపి వంటి తన పేర్లను చెబుతాడు. రుద్రుని ఆపడానికి నరుడు గడ్డి పరక తీసుకోగా అది గొప్ప గొడ్డలి అయిందని, ఉమాపతి హరునికి నమస్కరించమని అర్జునునికి చెబుతాడు.","ta":"சூரியனையும் சந்திரனையும் தன் முடியால் உருவாக்குவதாகக் கண்ணன் கூறி, விருஷாகபி போன்ற தன் பெயர்களைச் சொல்கிறான். ருத்ரனைத் தடுக்க நரன் புல்லை எடுத்தபோது அது பெரிய கோடரியானது என்றும், உமாபதி ஹரனை வணங்குமாறு அர்ஜுனனுக்கும் கூறுகிறான்.","ml":"തന്റെ മുടികൊണ്ട് താൻ സൂര്യനെയും ചന്ദ്രനെയും ഉണ്ടാക്കുന്നുവെന്ന് കൃഷ്ണൻ പറയുന്നു; വൃഷാകപി എന്നതുപോലെ തന്റെ അറിയപ്പെടുന്ന നാമങ്ങളും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. രുദ്രനെ തടയാൻ നരൻ ഒരു പുല്ലിൻതണ്ട് എടുത്തപ്പോൾ അത് വലിയ മഴുവായി മാറിയതെങ്ങനെയെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു; ഉമയുടെ നാഥനായ ഹരനെ നമസ്കരിക്കാൻ അർജുനനോട് പറഞ്ഞ് അദ്ദേഹം അവസാനിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.330; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"श्रीभगवानुवाच","meaning":{"en":"The Blessed Lord said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"सूर्याचन्द्रमसौ शश्वत्केशैर्मे अंशुसंज्ञितैः ।\nबोधयंस्तापयंश्चैव जगदुत्तिष्ठतः पृथक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With my rays, which are called my hair, I ceaselessly awaken and warm the world, as the sun and moon rise each in its own way."}},{"n":2,"text":"बोधनात्तापनाच्चैव जगतो हर्षणं भवेत् ।\nअग्नीषोमकृतैरेभिः कर्मभिः पाण्डुनन्दन ।\nहृषीकेशोऽहमीशानो वरदो लोकभावनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through awakening and warming, the world is gladdened. By these deeds done as Agni and Soma, son of Pandu, I am Hrishikesha, the lord, boon-giver, and nourisher of the worlds."}},{"n":3,"text":"इडोपहूतयोगेन हरे भागं क्रतुष्वहम् ।\nवर्णश्च मे हरिश्रेष्ठस्तस्माद्धरिरहं स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the rite of invoking Ida I take my share at sacrifices, and my color is that of the best of horses, the tawny one; therefore I am remembered as Hari."}},{"n":4,"text":"धाम सारो हि लोकानामृतं चैव विचारितम् ।\nऋतधामा ततो विप्रैः सत्यश्चाहं प्रकीर्तितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reflect: truth and nectar are the essence and abode of the worlds. Hence brahmins proclaim me Ritadhama, abode of truth, and also Satya."}},{"n":5,"text":"नष्टां च धरणीं पूर्वमविन्दं वै गुहागताम् ।\nगोविन्द इति मां देवा वाग्भिः समभितुष्टुवुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago I found the earth, lost and gone into a cave, and so the gods praised me in words as Govinda."}},{"n":6,"text":"शिपिविष्टेति चाख्यायां हीनरोमा च यो भवेत् ।\nतेनाविष्टं हि यत्किंचिच्छिपिविष्टं हि तत्स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shipivishta is the name for one who is hairless; whatever is pervaded by that is called shipivishta."}},{"n":7,"text":"यास्को मामृषिरव्यग्रो नैकयज्ञेषु गीतवान् ।\nशिपिविष्ट इति ह्यस्माद्गुह्यनामधरो ह्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The calm sage Yaska sang of me in many sacrifices as Shipivishta; so I bear that secret name."}},{"n":8,"text":"स्तुत्वा मां शिपिविष्टेति यास्को ऋषिरुदारधीः ।\nमत्प्रसादादधो नष्टं निरुक्तमभिजग्मिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By praising me as Shipivishta, the noble-minded sage Yaska, by my grace, recovered the Nirukta that had been lost below."}},{"n":9,"text":"न हि जातो न जायेऽहं न जनिष्ये कदाचन ।\nक्षेत्रज्ञः सर्वभूतानां तस्मादहमजः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I was never born, am not born, and never will be born; as the knower of the field in all beings I am called Aja, the unborn."}},{"n":10,"text":"नोक्तपूर्वं मया क्षुद्रमश्लीलं वा कदाचन ।\nऋता ब्रह्मसुता सा मे सत्या देवी सरस्वती ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have never spoken anything petty or coarse; the goddess Sarasvati, daughter of Brahma, true and orderly, is mine."}},{"n":11,"text":"सच्चासच्चैव कौन्तेय मयावेशितमात्मनि ।\nपौष्करे ब्रह्मसदने सत्यं मामृषयो विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Kunti, both being and non-being have been placed by me within myself. The sages know me as truth, in the Pushkara abode of Brahma."}},{"n":12,"text":"सत्त्वान्न च्युतपूर्वोऽहं सत्त्वं वै विद्धि मत्कृतम् ।\nजन्मनीहाभवत्सत्त्वं पौर्विकं मे धनंजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have never fallen from goodness; know that goodness is my making. Dhananjaya, in this birth goodness was mine from before."}},{"n":13,"text":"निराशीःकर्मसंयुक्तं सात्वतं मां प्रकल्पय ।\nसात्वतज्ञानदृष्टोऽहं सात्वतः सात्वतां पतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know me as Satvata, joined to action without desire for reward; I am seen through the knowledge of the Satvatas, a Satvata, lord of the Satvatas."}},{"n":14,"text":"कृषामि मेदिनीं पार्थ भूत्वा कार्ष्णायसो महान् ।\nकृष्णो वर्णश्च मे यस्मात्तस्मात्कृष्णोऽहमर्जुन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha, I till the earth, becoming a great iron plowshare; and because my color is dark, Arjuna, I am Krishna."}},{"n":15,"text":"मया संश्लेषिता भूमिरद्भिर्व्योम च वायुना ।\nवायुश्च तेजसा सार्धं वैकुण्ठत्वं ततो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"By me the earth was joined with water, the sky with wind, and wind with fire; hence my name Vaikuntha."}},{"n":16,"text":"निर्वाणं परमं सौख्यं धर्मोऽसौ पर उच्यते ।\nतस्मान्न च्युतपूर्वोऽहमच्युतस्तेन कर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Extinction is the highest bliss, and that is called supreme dharma. Since I have never fallen from it, by that act I am Achyuta."}},{"n":17,"text":"पृथिवीनभसी चोभे विश्रुते विश्वलौकिके ।\nतयोः संधारणार्थं हि मामधोक्षजमञ्जसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Earth and sky are both famed in all the world. To hold them up, I am rightly called Adhokshaja."}},{"n":18,"text":"निरुक्तं वेदविदुषो ये च शब्दार्थचिन्तकाः ।\nते मां गायन्ति प्राग्वंशे अधोक्षज इति स्थितिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who know the Vedas, who know Nirukta, and who ponder the meaning of words, sing me in the ancient lineage as Adhokshaja; so it stands."}},{"n":19,"text":"शब्द एकमतैरेष व्याहृतः परमर्षिभिः ।\nनान्यो ह्यधोक्षजो लोके ऋते नारायणं प्रभुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This word was proclaimed by the great sages in agreement; there is no other Adhokshaja in the world except the lord Narayana."}},{"n":20,"text":"घृतं ममार्चिषो लोके जन्तूनां प्राणधारणम् ।\nघृतार्चिरहमव्यग्रैर्वेदज्ञैः परिकीर्तितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ghee is my flames in the world, sustaining the breath of creatures; calm Vedic scholars call me Ghritarchis, \"ghee-flamed.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"त्रयो हि धातवः ख्याताः कर्मजा इति च स्मृताः ।\nपित्तं श्लेष्मा च वायुश्च एष संघात उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Three humors are declared, said to be born of action: bile, phlegm, and wind, called the combination."}},{"n":22,"text":"एतैश्च धार्यते जन्तुरेतैः क्षीणैश्च क्षीयते ।\nआयुर्वेदविदस्तस्मात्त्रिधातुं मां प्रचक्षते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through these a creature is sustained, and when they fail it fails; so those who know medicine call me Tridhatu."}},{"n":23,"text":"वृषो हि भगवान्धर्मः ख्यातो लोकेषु भारत ।\nनैघण्टुकपदाख्यातं विद्धि मां वृषमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, the blessed Dharma is known in the worlds as the bull, vrisha. Know me, by the word defined in the Nighantu, as the supreme Vrisha."}},{"n":24,"text":"कपिर्वराहः श्रेष्ठश्च धर्मश्च वृष उच्यते ।\nतस्माद्वृषाकपिं प्राह कश्यपो मां प्रजापतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kapi is the boar, the best, and Dharma is called vrisha; so the Prajapati Kashyapa calls me Vrishakapi."}},{"n":25,"text":"न चादिं न मध्यं तथा नैव चान्तं\nकदाचिद्विदन्ते सुराश्चासुराश्च ।\nअनाद्यो ह्यमध्यस्तथा चाप्यनन्तः\nप्रगीतोऽहमीशो विभुर्लोकसाक्षी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither gods nor asuras ever know my beginning, middle, or end. I am sung as without beginning, middle, or end: the lord, all-pervading witness of the worlds."}},{"n":26,"text":"शुचीनि श्रवणीयानि शृणोमीह धनंजय ।\nन च पापानि गृह्णामि ततोऽहं वै शुचिश्रवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya, I hear here what is pure and worth hearing, and I take in no evil; therefore I am Shuchishrava."}},{"n":27,"text":"एकशृङ्गः पुरा भूत्वा वराहो दिव्यदर्शनः ।\nइमामुद्धृतवान्भूमिमेकशृङ्गस्ततो ह्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago, as a boar of divine look with a single horn, I lifted this earth up; so I am Ekashringa."}},{"n":28,"text":"तथैवासं त्रिककुदो वाराहं रूपमास्थितः ।\nत्रिककुत्तेन विख्यातः शरीरस्य तु मापनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise I took a boar's form with three humps, and was known as Trikakut from the measuring of the body."}},{"n":29,"text":"विरिञ्च इति यः प्रोक्तः कपिलज्ञानचिन्तकैः ।\nस प्रजापतिरेवाहं चेतनात्सर्वलोककृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The one called Virinchi by those who contemplate Kapila's knowledge is I, the Prajapati, maker of all worlds through consciousness."}},{"n":30,"text":"विद्यासहायवन्तं मामादित्यस्थं सनातनम् ।\nकपिलं प्राहुराचार्याः सांख्या निश्चितनिश्चयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Samkhya teachers, firm in their conclusions, call me Kapila, eternal, dwelling in the sun, with knowledge as my aid."}},{"n":31,"text":"हिरण्यगर्भो द्युतिमानेष यश्छन्दसि स्तुतः ।\nयोगैः संपूज्यते नित्यं स एवाहं विभुः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who is praised in the Vedic meters as the radiant Hiranyagarbha, and always worshipped by the yogas, I too am remembered as that all-pervader."}},{"n":32,"text":"एकविंशतिशाखं च ऋग्वेदं मां प्रचक्षते ।\nसहस्रशाखं यत्साम ये वै वेदविदो जनाः ।\nगायन्त्यारण्यके विप्रा मद्भक्तास्तेऽपि दुर्लभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They call me the Rig Veda of twenty-one branches, and the Sama of a thousand branches that the Veda-knowing brahmins sing in the Aranyaka; even those devotees of mine are rare."}},{"n":33,"text":"षट्पञ्चाशतमष्टौ च सप्तत्रिंशतमित्युत ।\nयस्मिञ्शाखा यजुर्वेदे सोऽहमाध्वर्यवे स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Yajur Veda, in which branches number fifty-six, eight, and thirty-seven, I am remembered as in the adhvaryu priest's rites."}},{"n":34,"text":"पञ्चकल्पमथर्वाणं कृत्याभिः परिबृंहितम् ।\nकल्पयन्ति हि मां विप्रा अथर्वाणविदस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins versed in the Atharvan, of five kalpas and enriched with spells, understand me in that way."}},{"n":35,"text":"शाखाभेदाश्च ये केचिद्याश्च शाखासु गीतयः ।\nस्वरवर्णसमुच्चाराः सर्वांस्तान्विद्धि मत्कृतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever differences of branches there are, the songs in the branches, and the pronunciations of tone and letter, know all of them as made by me."}},{"n":36,"text":"यत्तद्धयशिरः पार्थ समुदेति वरप्रदम् ।\nसोऽहमेवोत्तरे भागे क्रमाक्षरविभागवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha, the horse-headed boon-giver who arises, I am that one; and in the later portion I know the division of sequence and syllables."}},{"n":37,"text":"रामादेशितमार्गेण मत्प्रसादान्महात्मना ।\nपाञ्चालेन क्रमः प्राप्तस्तस्माद्भूतात्सनातनात् ।\nबाभ्रव्यगोत्रः स बभौ प्रथमः क्रमपारगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the path Rama showed, by my grace, the Panchala, the great one, obtained the Krama from that eternal being; he of Babhravya's line shone as the first master of the Krama."}},{"n":38,"text":"नारायणाद्वरं लब्ध्वा प्राप्य योगमनुत्तमम् ।\nक्रमं प्रणीय शिक्षां च प्रणयित्वा स गालवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having received a boon from Narayana and attained the highest yoga, Galava composed the Krama and the Shiksha."}},{"n":39,"text":"कण्डरीकोऽथ राजा च ब्रह्मदत्तः प्रतापवान् ।\nजातीमरणजं दुःखं स्मृत्वा स्मृत्वा पुनः पुनः ।\nसप्तजातिषु मुख्यत्वाद्योगानां संपदं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Kandarika and the mighty Brahmadatta, remembering again and again the pain of birth and death, reached the wealth of yoga through being foremost in seven births."}},{"n":40,"text":"पुराहमात्मजः पार्थ प्रथितः कारणान्तरे ।\nधर्मस्य कुरुशार्दूल ततोऽहं धर्मजः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha, in the past I became famed as Dharma's own son for a certain reason, tiger of the Kurus; hence I am remembered as Dharmaja."}},{"n":41,"text":"नरनारायणौ पूर्वं तपस्तेपतुरव्ययम् ।\nधर्मयानं समारूढौ पर्वते गन्धमादने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nara and Narayana, mounted on the chariot of dharma, once practiced imperishable austerity on Mount Gandhamadana."}},{"n":42,"text":"तत्कालसमयं चैव दक्षयज्ञो बभूव ह ।\nन चैवाकल्पयद्भागं दक्षो रुद्रस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that time Daksha's sacrifice took place, and Daksha did not allot a share to Rudra, Bharata."}},{"n":43,"text":"ततो दधीचिवचनाद्दक्षयज्ञमपाहरत् ।\nससर्ज शूलं क्रोधेन प्रज्वलन्तं मुहुर्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, on Dadhichi's word, Rudra broke up Daksha's sacrifice and, in anger, hurled a spear that blazed again and again."}},{"n":44,"text":"तच्छूलं भस्मसात्कृत्वा दक्षयज्ञं सविस्तरम् ।\nआवयोः सहसागच्छद्बदर्याश्रममन्तिकात् ।\nवेगेन महता पार्थ पतन्नारायणोरसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having reduced Daksha's whole sacrifice to ashes, that spear suddenly came toward us, near the Badari hermitage, and with great speed, Partha, fell on Narayana's chest."}},{"n":45,"text":"ततः स्वतेजसाविष्टाः केशा नारायणस्य ह ।\nबभूवुर्मुञ्जवर्णास्तु ततोऽहं मुञ्जकेशवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Narayana's hair, filled with his own radiance, became the color of munja grass; therefore I am Munjakeshavan."}},{"n":46,"text":"तच्च शूलं विनिर्धूतं हुंकारेण महात्मना ।\nजगाम शंकरकरं नारायणसमाहतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That spear, shaken off by the great one's roar, struck by Narayana, went back to Shankara's hand."}},{"n":47,"text":"अथ रुद्र उपाधावत्तावृषी तपसान्वितौ ।\nतत एनं समुद्धूतं कण्ठे जग्राह पाणिना ।\nनारायणः स विश्वात्मा तेनास्य शितिकण्ठता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Rudra rushed at the two sages rich in austerity, and Narayana, soul of the universe, seized him by the throat with his hand as he rose up; thereby his throat is blue."}},{"n":48,"text":"अथ रुद्रविघातार्थमिषीकां जगृहे नरः ।\nमन्त्रैश्च संयुयोजाशु सोऽभवत्परशुर्महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Nara took up a blade of reed to strike Rudra and quickly charged it with mantras; it became a great axe."}},{"n":49,"text":"क्षिप्तश्च सहसा रुद्रे खण्डनं प्राप्तवांस्तदा ।\nततोऽहं खण्डपरशुः स्मृतः परशुखण्डनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hurled suddenly at Rudra, it was broken; hence I am called Khandaparashu, from the breaking of the axe."}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":50,"text":"अस्मिन्युद्धे तु वार्ष्णेय त्रैलोक्यमथने तदा ।\nजयं कः प्राप्तवांस्तत्र शंसैतन्मे जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vrishni's son, in that battle that churned the three worlds, who gained victory? Tell me this, Janardana."}},{"text":"श्रीभगवानुवाच","meaning":{"en":"The Blessed Lord said:"}},{"n":51,"text":"तयोः संलग्नयोर्युद्धे रुद्रनारायणात्मनोः ।\nउद्विग्नाः सहसा कृत्स्ना लोकाः सर्वेऽभवंस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Rudra and Narayana were locked in battle, all the worlds were suddenly thrown into turmoil."}},{"n":52,"text":"नागृह्णात्पावकः शुभ्रं मखेषु सुहुतं हविः ।\nवेदा न प्रतिभान्ति स्म ऋषीणां भावितात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fire did not accept the bright oblation well offered in sacrifices, and the Vedas did not shine for the sages of purified souls."}},{"n":53,"text":"देवान्रजस्तमश्चैव समाविविशतुस्तदा ।\nवसुधा संचकम्पेऽथ नभश्च विपफाल ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Passion and darkness entered the gods, the earth trembled, and the sky split."}},{"n":54,"text":"निष्प्रभाणि च तेजांसि ब्रह्मा चैवासनाच्च्युतः ।\nअगाच्छोषं समुद्रश्च हिमवांश्च व्यशीर्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lights lost their brilliance, Brahma fell from his seat, the ocean dried up, and the Himalaya crumbled."}},{"n":55,"text":"तस्मिन्नेवं समुत्पन्ने निमित्ते पाण्डुनन्दन ।\nब्रह्मा वृतो देवगणैरृषिभिश्च महात्मभिः ।\nआजगामाशु तं देशं यत्र युद्धमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"When such omens arose, son of Pandu, Brahma, surrounded by troops of gods and great sages, quickly came to the place where the battle raged."}},{"n":56,"text":"साञ्जलिप्रग्रहो भूत्वा चतुर्वक्त्रो निरुक्तगः ।\nउवाच वचनं रुद्रं लोकानामस्तु वै शिवम् ।\nन्यस्यायुधानि विश्वेश जगतो हितकाम्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"With folded hands, the four-faced one, true to the explanations, said to Rudra: \"May it be well for the worlds. Lord of the universe, lay down your weapons for the world's good."}},{"n":57,"text":"यदक्षरमथाव्यक्तमीशं लोकस्य भावनम् ।\nकूटस्थं कर्तृनिर्द्वंद्वमकर्तेति च यं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whom they call the imperishable, the unmanifest, the lord, the world's source, the unchanging, the doer beyond the pairs, and also the non-doer,"}},{"n":58,"text":"व्यक्तिभावगतस्यास्य एका मूर्तिरियं शिवा ।\nनरो नारायणश्चैव जातौ धर्मकुलोद्वहौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"this auspicious one form of him, come into manifestation, is Nara and Narayana, born to bear Dharma's lineage."}},{"n":59,"text":"तपसा महता युक्तौ देवश्रेष्ठौ महाव्रतौ ।\nअहं प्रसादजस्तस्य कस्मिंश्चित्कारणान्तरे ।\nत्वं चैव क्रोधजस्तात पूर्वसर्गे सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Joined with great austerity, best of gods, of great vows: I am born of his grace for a certain purpose, and you, dear one, are born of his wrath, in a former creation, eternal."}},{"n":60,"text":"मया च सार्धं वरदं विबुधैश्च महर्षिभिः ।\nप्रसादयाशु लोकानां शान्तिर्भवतु माचिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With me and the gods and great sages, propitiate the boon-giver quickly, so that peace may come to the worlds without delay.\""}},{"n":61,"text":"ब्रह्मणा त्वेवमुक्तस्तु रुद्रः क्रोधाग्निमुत्सृजन् ।\nप्रसादयामास ततो देवं नारायणं प्रभुम् ।\nशरणं च जगामाद्यं वरेण्यं वरदं हरिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told this by Brahma, Rudra let go his fire of anger and propitiated the lord God Narayana, going for refuge to Hari, the primal, choicest giver of boons."}},{"n":62,"text":"ततोऽथ वरदो देवो जितक्रोधो जितेन्द्रियः ।\nप्रीतिमानभवत्तत्र रुद्रेण सह संगतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the boon-giving god, having conquered anger and senses, became pleased, meeting Rudra."}},{"n":63,"text":"ऋषिभिर्ब्रह्मणा चैव विबुधैश्च सुपूजितः ।\nउवाच देवमीशानमीशः स जगतो हरिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Well honored by the sages, Brahma, and the gods, Hari, lord of the world, spoke to the god Ishana."}},{"n":64,"text":"यस्त्वां वेत्ति स मां वेत्ति यस्त्वामनु स मामनु ।\nनावयोरन्तरं किंचिन्मा ते भूद्बुद्धिरन्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Whoever knows you knows me; whoever follows you follows me. There is no difference between us. Let your mind not think otherwise."}},{"n":65,"text":"अद्य प्रभृति श्रीवत्सः शूलाङ्कोऽयं भवत्वयम् ।\nमम पाण्यङ्कितश्चापि श्रीकण्ठस्त्वं भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"From today, let this mark be the Shrivatsa and the spear sign on me, and you, marked by my hand, will be Shrikantha."}},{"n":66,"text":"एवं लक्षणमुत्पाद्य परस्परकृतं तदा ।\nसख्यं चैवातुलं कृत्वा रुद्रेण सहितावृषी ।\nतपस्तेपतुरव्यग्रौ विसृज्य त्रिदिवौकसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, having made these marks on each other and sealed an unequaled friendship, the two sages, with Rudra, dismissed the dwellers of heaven and calmly resumed austerity."}},{"n":67,"text":"एष ते कथितः पार्थ नारायणजयो मृधे ।\nनामानि चैव गुह्यानि निरुक्तानि च भारत ।\nऋषिभिः कथितानीह यानि संकीर्तितानि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha, I have told you of Narayana's victory in battle, and of the secret names and their meanings, which the sages have recited here."}},{"n":68,"text":"एवं बहुविधै रूपैश्चरामीह वसुंधराम् ।\nब्रह्मलोकं च कौन्तेय गोलोकं च सनातनम् ।\nमया त्वं रक्षितो युद्धे महान्तं प्राप्तवाञ्जयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In such manifold forms I move on earth, and in Brahma's world and the eternal Goloka, son of Kunti. Protected by me in battle, you won a great victory."}},{"n":69,"text":"यस्तु ते सोऽग्रतो याति युद्धे संप्रत्युपस्थिते ।\nतं विद्धि रुद्रं कौन्तेय देवदेवं कपर्दिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know that the one who goes before you in battle, when it is joined, is Rudra, the god of gods, with matted hair."}},{"n":70,"text":"कालः स एव कथितः क्रोधजेति मया तव ।\nनिहतांस्तेन वै पूर्वं हतवानसि वै रिपून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I told you of Kala, born of wrath; those you killed were first slain by him."}},{"n":71,"text":"अप्रमेयप्रभावं तं देवदेवमुमापतिम् ।\nनमस्व देवं प्रयतो विश्वेशं हरमव्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bow with discipline to that god of limitless power, the god of gods, husband of Uma, lord of the universe, Hara, the imperishable."}}]}]}